 a well dressed man is sitting on a rock, next to the village’s entrance, looking downcast; he is eyeing you… quietly judging….
- you ignore him
	noble: hold on traveler, if a knight like you happens to come to our village, he must his reasons to, mind sharing your travel with this humble peasant?
- you move towards him
	noble: well well, a wandering knight coming to our humble village, may i ask what’s your business with us?
noble: ha, you speak of the giant! he is indeed a terrible foe, and one that wont be lured out so easily,your journey will be precious… but you will find what you seek traveler.
noble: if… during your travels in this land you could find it in your heart to help the poor people of this village, i would be most indebted to you, ho wandering knight
